    {
      "sourceUrl": "https://profiles.ucsd.edu/kevin.corbett",
      "observedAt": "2026-10-07T22:08:57+00:00",
      "text": "Our lab is focused on the molecular mechanisms of chromosome segregation in meiosis. We use biochemistry, X-ray crystallography, and genetics in S. cerevisiae to probe the structure, function, and interactions between proteins involved in meiotic chromosome pairing, crossover initiation and maturation, and chromosome segregation. A new focus involves the structure and function of the first identified bacterial HORMA domain proteins, a family of signaling proteins previously thought to exist only in eukaryotes.",
      "title": "Associated faculty research: Kevin D. Corbett",
